# MC-X-F12 (writer 9), the ask path. L §4.3: "An ask line that reads a law-dated input or band directly ... states
# `law D`". rate's rows all govern always, so it isn't law-dated ("A fact is law-dated when its value can change with the law date: an input, band, def or rule with a row or version whose span isn't `always`"),
# and q needs no law. snap12: LOAD-LAWDATE ask q reads law-dated rate directly, without law.
=== m.tally
model f12c
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "MC-X-F12, the ask path: an ask line reads a band whose every row governs always, with no law (L 4.3: not law-dated)."

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

source act "the act"


input age3: int

band rate(a: int): money PLN



ask q: rate(age3)

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  age3 = 3 "the age"
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
=== expect
q: 400.00 PLN
  cut 2027-12-31
